10237	{"artifactId":"LLD-06f196a7ff528143-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-06f196a7ff528143-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-21T08:07:22.963Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers the upstream ISSUE's requested scope: Story-attributed review, diff-only grounding, BUILD change logs, and reporting excluded edits.","evidence":"The ISSUE's Fix intent explicitly names those three consumers and exclusion reporting. Inspected implementations anchor the subject and diff grounding on the Story key; both BUILD writers forward that key; the review runner persists excludedFromScope. [files: docs/standalone/scope-story-s-code-review-what-E20261021b97752e9/ISSUE.md, src/workflow/code-review/subject.ts, src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts, src/workflow/code-review/runner.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/completion-record.ts, src/daemon/steps/build-step/phases/validate.ts]","action":"Preserve this scope while completing the remaining amendments.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The migration amendment correctly distinguishes implemented scoping from the remaining legacy-end, stable-commit, and rename-parser work.","evidence":"changedFiles already reads storyChangeSet before working-tree diffs. storyChangeSet still enumerates 'base..HEAD' without a recorded-end bound. persistBuildRecord computes 'rec.body.commit ?? storyCommit(...) ?? headShortSha(repoPath)'. buildStatArgv lacks '-z', and parseNumstat splits lines and matches ' => '. These match the amendment's stated remaining work. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/changed-files.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/story-commits.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/diff.ts]","action":"Keep the historical State before text distinct from the current implementation status.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The legacy-end amendment can reuse existing BUILD identity and persistence infrastructure while adding a distinct range-end resolver.","evidence":"range-base.ts already reads BUILD JSON through ARTIFACTS_DIR and buildArtifactId, and provides synchronous, non-throwing range-base resolution. Its full implementation contains no range-end resolver; repository search found no resolveStoryRangeEnd. standalone-record.ts already centralizes both writers through persistBuildRecord and has a prior-record reader. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/range-base.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts]","action":"Reuse the existing identity and read helpers; preserve the proposed non-throwing resolver contract.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The identified production callers supply Story identity to degraded grounding and validation selection.","evidence":"Both code-review-rpc.ts and beginDiffOnlyReview pass base, LEDGER_EXCLUDE_GLOBS, and storyKey to the grounding assembler. validate.ts has one withTypecheckProjects call in runValidateSession and one trivialCheckPlan call in the standalone branch, both forwarding the Story key. [files: src/daemon/code-review-rpc.ts, src/daemon/steps/code-review-step/handler.ts, src/daemon/steps/build-step/phases/validate.ts, src/daemon/steps/build-step/validation-checks.ts]","action":"Retain both degraded-review callers and both validation selection sites in regression coverage.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Changing numstat to NUL-delimited literal paths is sufficient to make every reported path agree with the per-file hunk lookup, including paths containing tabs.","evidence":"splitDiffByFile still matches only '/^diff --git a\\/(.+?) b\\/(.+?)\\s*$/m'. Git quotes headers for tab-containing paths, such as 'diff --git \"a/src/a\\\\tb.ts\" \"b/src/a\\\\tb.ts\"'; a read-only evaluation confirmed this header does not match. buildDiffSymbols then substitutes '[no hunk text for ...]'. The proposed numstat parser fixes file identity but leaves these files without review hunks. [files: src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/diff.ts, src/workflow/code-review/__tests__/diff-attribution.test.ts]","action":"Extend the design to decode Git-quoted diff-header paths and use literal names consistently for hunk lookup. Add an end-to-end rename test with a tab-containing path and committed, staged, and unstaged hunks.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An explicitly empty new BUILD changeLog replaces contaminated prior data, while the rendered Changes section remains absent.","evidence":"Both BUILD writers supply changeLog unconditionally. mergeWithPrior spreads '...prior.body, ...rec.body'. renderBuildRecordMd renders Changes through an omit-slot section. The inspected rewrite test asserts both an empty stored changeLog and absence of '## Changes'. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/completion-record.ts, src/daemon/steps/build-step/phases/validate.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/__tests__/changed-files.test.ts]","action":"Preserve unconditional writes of empty changeLog values.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Review-record exclusion metadata is additive, and legacy working-tree attribution remains representable.","evidence":"CodeReviewSubject and CodeReviewBody.subject declare excludedFromScope optional. ChangeSetAttribution retains 'working-tree'. The runner includes excludedFromScope only when its length is positive; the inspected runner test checks JSON persistence and omission for both undefined and empty arrays. [files: src/workflow/code-review/types.ts, src/workflow/code-review/runner.ts, src/workflow/code-review/__tests__/runner.test.ts]","action":"Keep the optional field and legacy attribution union.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The change belongs to a standalone Story and extends existing shared implementations without introducing a separate IPC scoping contract.","evidence":"The persisted LLD metadata marks the work standalone. The inspected production paths reuse changedFiles, storyChangeSet, the grounding assembler, and persistBuildRecord. Story identity already travels through the existing code-review and validate entry points; the proposed helpers and options are internal. [files: .insrc/artifacts/LLD-06f196a7ff528143-s1.json, src/workflow/runners/build/changed-files.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/story-commits.ts, src/daemon/code-review-rpc.ts, src/daemon/steps/build-step/phases/validate.ts]","action":"Keep attribution logic centralized in the existing shared derivation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Missing anchors and failed Git reads propagate through the stated refusal paths instead of widening scope.","evidence":"changedFiles rejects storyKey without base. Strict scanTrailers rethrows Git failures. resolveCodeReviewSubject returns no-build-record for missing base or NoBuildChangesError. Grounding wraps change-set failures as DiffUnavailableError; runDiff and collectDiff reject unsuccessful git_diff results. git_diff already rejects numstat failures. collectBuildChangeLog catches derivation failures and returns []. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/changed-files.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/story-commits.ts, src/workflow/code-review/subject.ts, src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/diff.ts]","action":"Apply these same failure semantics to the remaining amendments.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design maps ac1–ac5 to concrete regression tests or a specified installed-daemon smoke.","evidence":"The mapping covers exclusion reporting, own-file edits, refusal paths, downstream consumers, and the observed daemon case. Inspected test bodies assert subject exclusions, strict-scan refusal, committed plus staged/unstaged hunks, filtered legacy diffs, empty changeLog replacement, and Story-scoped validation projects. Legacy-end and rename tests are proposed remaining work. Tests were inspected, not executed; the installed-daemon smoke is not established as passing. [files: docs/standalone/scope-story-s-code-review-what-E2026102106f196a7/S001/LLD.md, src/workflow/runners/build/__tests__/changed-files.test.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/__tests__/story-commits-trailer.test.ts, src/workflow/code-review/__tests__/subject-attribution.test.ts, src/workflow/code-review/__tests__/diff-attribution.test.ts, src/daemon/steps/build-step/__tests__/validation-checks.test.ts]","action":"Implement the remaining mapped tests and smoke, and add the quoted-path regression identified under change-sites. Test execution requires a writable environment because these suites create temporary repositories.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":0,"low":9,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-21T08:07:22.963Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6-astra","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
